WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:14.339
At dinner Mr.

2
00:00:14.359 --> 00:00:16.020
Havisham was lost in thought.

3
00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:22.302
He ate hardly anything, and whenever anyone spoke to him, he seemed startled.

4
00:00:22.322 --> 00:00:25.763
"What?" he said more than once.

5
00:00:27.763 --> 00:00:30.784
Cedric, who was sitting next to the earl, smiled at the lawyer.

6
00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:32.441
But Mr.

7
00:00:32.461 --> 00:00:34.823
Havisham just gave him an anxious glance.

8
00:00:34.843 --> 00:00:38.005
"Something's wrong with my friend Mr.

9
00:00:38.065 --> 00:00:39.907
Havisham," Cedric thought.

10
00:00:39.927 --> 00:00:42.369
"He always smiles at me.

11
00:00:42.389 --> 00:00:45.312
I hate to see him so worried."

12
00:00:46.493 --> 00:00:47.373
Meanwhile Mr.

13
00:00:47.413 --> 00:00:51.357
Havisham felt more distressed every time he looked at Cedric and the earl.

14
00:00:51.377 --> 00:00:55.300
"What terrible news I have to give them!"

15
00:00:55.801 --> 00:00:56.361
he thought.

16
00:00:56.381 --> 00:00:59.504
"It will ruin their lives forever."

17
00:01:01.968 --> 00:01:04.710
After dinner Cedric joined the ladies in the drawing room.

18
00:01:05.991 --> 00:01:08.012
The men stayed in the dining room to talk.

19
00:01:09.273 --> 00:01:11.234
The earl raised his eyebrows at Mr.

20
00:01:11.254 --> 00:01:13.196
Havisham, inviting him to speak.

21
00:01:14.376 --> 00:01:15.737
But the lawyer shook his head.

22
00:01:15.757 --> 00:01:18.939
"Not yet," he whispered.

23
00:01:22.121 --> 00:01:25.704
By the time the men joined the ladies, Cedric was sleepy.

24
00:01:29.084 --> 00:01:32.626
Leaning back on a soft sofa cushion, he closed his eyes.

25
00:01:33.787 --> 00:01:36.728
He vaguely heard guests saying goodnight to the earl.

26
00:01:38.769 --> 00:01:41.931
The earl had been growing more and more uneasy.

27
00:01:43.072 --> 00:01:46.313
And when he was uneasy, he was always in a bad mood.

28
00:01:48.355 --> 00:01:51.176
After the last guest had left, he turned on Mr.

29
00:01:51.196 --> 00:01:54.898
Havisham. "Well, what's this news that you've brought me?

30
00:01:54.918 --> 00:01:57.900
And why have you made me wait all evening?"

31
00:02:00.828 --> 00:02:03.609
"It's bad news, my lord," Mr.

32
00:02:03.629 --> 00:02:06.550
Havisham said carefully as the two men sat down.

33
00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:08.930
"The worst news.

34
00:02:09.570 --> 00:02:11.951
And I'm sorry to be the bearer of it."

35
00:02:13.191 --> 00:02:18.893
Mr. Havisham glanced over at Cedric, who was asleep and unaware that his life was about to change.

36
00:02:18.913 --> 00:02:23.014
"Why do you keep looking at the boy like that?"

37
00:02:23.414 --> 00:02:24.514
the earl demanded.

38
00:02:24.534 --> 00:02:27.355
"I saw you watching him at dinner.

39
00:02:28.335 --> 00:02:30.116
What does your news have to do with him?"

40
00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:35.283
"It has everything to do with Lord Fauntleroy," Mr.

41
00:02:35.323 --> 00:02:36.224
Havisham said.

42
00:02:36.244 --> 00:02:40.568
"I was late tonight because a woman came to see me.

43
00:02:42.169 --> 00:02:45.011
She told me an extraordinary story."

44
00:02:46.172 --> 00:02:49.495
Mr. Havisham paused before making his dramatic announcement.

45
00:02:49.515 --> 00:02:55.801
"It seems that Cedric is not the real Lord Fauntleroy!"

46
00:02:55.821 --> 00:02:58.583
"That's nonsense!"

47
00:03:00.116 --> 00:03:01.277
The earl snorted.

48
00:03:01.297 --> 00:03:05.301
"Of course he's the real Lord Fauntleroy."

49
00:03:06.902 --> 00:03:09.284
Mr. Havisham looked over at Cedric again.

50
00:03:09.304 --> 00:03:16.671
"The real Lord Fauntleroy is the son of your older son, Bevis.

51
00:03:17.672 --> 00:03:22.196
At the moment he's staying with his American mother at an inn in the village."

52
00:03:24.078 --> 00:03:26.340
The earl gripped the arms of his chair.

53
00:03:27.656 --> 00:03:30.137
Veins stood out on his hands and his forehead.

54
00:03:30.157 --> 00:03:32.777
"Who told you this lie?"

55
00:03:33.118 --> 00:03:34.098
he said angrily.

56
00:03:34.118 --> 00:03:37.799
"Bevis didn't have any children when he died."

57
00:03:37.819 --> 00:03:41.840
"That's what we thought," Mr.

58
00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:42.780
Havisham said.

59
00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:48.102
"But this woman said Bevis married her six years ago in London.

60
00:03:49.162 --> 00:03:52.823
She showed me her marriage certificate, which appears to be real.

61
00:03:53.923 --> 00:03:56.924
Then she said she had a five-year-old son."

62
00:03:58.728 --> 00:04:01.770
The earl was too shocked to say anything, so Mr.

63
00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:02.911
Havisham went on.

64
00:04:02.931 --> 00:04:08.834
"Soon after the boy's birth, Bevis and this woman decided to separate.

65
00:04:09.595 --> 00:04:12.076
He paid her a sum of money to disappear."

66
00:04:12.096 --> 00:04:17.119
"That sounds like something Bevis would do," the earl admitted.

67
00:04:17.139 --> 00:04:22.642
"He was always irresponsible, a total disgrace to the family.

68
00:04:23.763 --> 00:04:25.024
What is this woman like?"

69
00:04:26.264 --> 00:04:29.886
"For a while she didn't realize what her son was entitled to.

70
00:04:30.946 --> 00:04:36.149
But she recently consulted a lawyer and learned that the boy is your heir."

71
00:04:37.129 --> 00:04:38.170
The lawyer shuddered.

72
00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:44.513
"She's uneducated, totally greedy, and only cares about money."

73
00:04:45.993 --> 00:04:48.535
The earl took out his handkerchief and mopped his face.

74
00:04:49.735 --> 00:04:51.196
He gestured toward Cedric.

75
00:04:52.736 --> 00:04:55.997
"And to think that I objected to this dear boy's mother.

76
00:04:57.097 --> 00:05:01.639
I took her child away and then refused to have anything to do with her."

77
00:05:02.979 --> 00:05:04.179
The earl shook his head.

78
00:05:04.199 --> 00:05:09.741
"I suppose this is my punishment," he said bitterly.

79
00:05:11.801 --> 00:05:14.842
Suddenly he rose from his chair and began to pace the room.

80
00:05:17.223 --> 00:05:20.384
He raged about Bevis and his horrible American wife.

81
00:05:21.408 --> 00:05:23.750
But he never spoke loudly enough to wake Cedric.

82
00:05:24.911 --> 00:05:29.875
Broken and haggard, the earl approached the sofa and stood over Cedric.

83
00:05:29.895 --> 00:05:36.240
"If anyone had told me I could be fond of a child, I wouldn't have believed them.

84
00:05:36.260 --> 00:05:40.824
I always disliked children, especially my own.

85
00:05:42.445 --> 00:05:45.988
But I am fond of this one, and he is fond of me."

86
00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:51.569
The earl brushed the hair from Cedric's forehead, and the boy stirred.

87
00:05:51.589 --> 00:05:56.631
"Cedric would've been a better earl than I've been.

88
00:05:57.812 --> 00:06:00.954
No one would've called him the 'wicked Earl of Dorincourt.'

89
00:06:01.174 --> 00:06:03.936
He would've brought honor to the family."

90
00:06:05.036 --> 00:06:09.879
For a moment the earl bent down and studied Cedric's happy, sleeping face.

91
00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:13.041
Then he rang for a footman.

92
00:06:14.301 --> 00:06:17.183
When the footman appeared, the earl pointed to the sofa.

93
00:06:19.288 --> 00:06:21.493
"Carry—" The earl's voice cracked with emotion.

94
00:06:21.513 --> 00:06:24.959
"Carry Lord Fauntleroy to his room."
